    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/4053746/adjunct-faculty-c-h-lute-school-of-business": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, C.H. Lute School of Business",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, C.H. Lute School of Business Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-Adjunct Business Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA - School of Business Opening Date 07/10/2026 Description Benefits Job Description Summary The College of Professional Studies at Shawnee State University seeks qualified individuals beginning Fall and Spring Semesters to serve as Part-time Faculty (Adjunct) in the C.H. Lute School of Business for the classes listed below: Accounting Information Systems Management Management Marketing Sport Management Master of Business Administration Note to Applicants for online teaching opportunities: Preference is given to individuals with formal training and/or previous experience in online delivery of courses. Minimum Qualifications (EDUCATION, KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES, and EXPERIENCE) Master’s degree in the respective or related area (doctorate required to teach in MBA program) Excellent communication skills and ability to communicate effectively with students from diverse backgrounds Familiarity with and ability to utilize existing and emerging technology in teaching Ability to use collaborative learning techniques and student-centered methods of instruction Ability to work in a multi-ethnic/multicultural environment Ability/willingness to work a flexible schedule that may include evening and weekend assignments – daytime availability a plus (in some cases, may be required) Certification and/or experience with online instruction necessary for online assignments. Applications are accepted on a continuous basis. Interested candidates must apply online to this Posting (only online applications will be accepted). Complete your application by clicking the Apply for this Job link above and including: a cover letter addressed to Dr. Jason Lovins, Director, C.H. Lute School of Business , specifically addressing how your qualifications meet the posted minimum requirements of the position; your resume/vitae (including relevant professional experience); and your unofficial transcripts indicating highest degree attained. Candidates invited for an on-campus interview may be required to present a teaching lecture and laboratory demonstration of their instructional abilities. Specific questions regarding courses may be directed to the Dean’s office. at 740.351.3270. Stipend is based on contact hour basis according to the highest degree held. Employment with the University is dependent upon BOT budget approval for the current fiscal year. Background check is required prior to hire. Official transcripts are required and must be submitted prior to hire to the Dean’s Office, College of Business and Engineering Technology at 940 2nd Street Portsmouth, OH 45662 Note to Applicants for online teaching opportunities: Preference is given to individuals with formal training and/or previous experience in online delivery of courses. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/4151594/adjunct-faculty-fine-digital-performing-arts": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-034 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-CAS-Fine, Digital & Performing Arts Opening Date 04/20/2026 Closing Date 1/10/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary Job Description Summary The Department of Fine, Digital, and Performing Arts invites applications for all semesters for part-time adjunct teaching positions. These are semester-to-semester positions primarily teaching introductory sections of the following areas, both in person and online. Acting Art History Audio Design Ceramics Dance Digital 3D Drawing Figure Drawing Game Development Arts Graphic Arts Musical Theatre Painting Photography Piano lessons The Department of Fine, Digital, and Performing Arts at Shawnee State is an incubator for creativity. Majors, Minors, and GEP courses in the arts enable students to cultivate and expand their skills across several arts disciplines. The department faculty value technical skill, aesthetic dialogue, professionalism, open individual expression, and reasoned critique. Applications are accepted continuously. All applicants must complete the online application at Shawnee.edu . Upload a cover letter to Human Resources specifically addressing how your qualifications meet the posted qualifications Your resume/curriculum vitae (including a link to a portfolio of relevant work), and An unofficial transcript indicating the highest degree attained. IMPORTANT NOTE ABOUT REFERENCE SECTION : Include the name, email address, and phone number of your Professional References. Candidates invited for an on-campus interview may be required to deliver a teaching lecture and a laboratory demonstration to demonstrate their instructional abilities. Specific questions may be directed to Dr. Greg Lyons, Chair of the Department of Fine, Digital, and Performing Arts at 740.351.3004. Adjunct faculty at SSU are also eligible for tuition waivers ( Tuition Waiver for Adjunct Faculty Policy ) and enjoy professional development opportunities, office space, and limited mileage reimbursement. They and their family (children 14 years and up) also have free access to the Rhodes Athletic Facility. Employment with the University is dependent upon BOT budget approval for the current fiscal year. A background check is required prior to hire. Official transcripts are required and must be submitted prior to hire to Dr. Michael Barnhart, Interim Dean of the College of Arts & Sciences at 940 2nd Street, Portsmouth, OH 45662. Note to Applicants - This is an open posting maintained and updated every semester based upon the enrollment needs of the Department and, as such, is filled on an as-needed/ongoing basis every semester. SSU seeks individuals who share our commitment to students as our first priority. Shawnee State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against any individual because of race, color, genetic information, religion, age, disability, national origin, ancestry, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, veteran status or military status. Minimum Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (EDUCATION, KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES, AND EXPERIENCE) Master’s Degree in the subject or closely related area A willingness to engage students thoughtfully and critically in the subject area Ability to communicate clearly to students Basic knowledge of instructional software and ability to teach online courses Ability to work closely and effectively with diverse populations in all aspects PREFERRED QUALIFICATION Knowledge of different pedagogical strategies Prior teaching experience both in person and online MFA or PhD in the area being taught or closely related area This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/4207331/adjunct-faculty-engineering-technologies": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Engineering Technologies",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Engineering Technologies Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-032 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-Engineering Technologies Opening Date 06/08/2026 Closing Date 4/4/2027 4:00 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary Job Description The College of Business and Engineering Technology at Shawnee State University is seeking qualified individuals beginning Fall Semester to serve as Part-time Faculty (Adjunct) in the Department of Engineering Technologies. The Department of Engineering Technologies offers a diverse set of programs/courses in the areas listed below: Computer Aided Design & Manufacturing Technology (CAD) Computer Engineering Technology Digital Simulation & Gaming Electromechanical Engineering Technology Information Security Plastics Engineering Technology Machine Tools Applications are accepted on a continuous basis. All applicants must complete the online application. Upload a cover letter to Human Resources specifically addressing how your qualifications meet the posted qualifications. Your resume/curriculum vitae, Uno fficial transcript indicating highest degree attained IMPORTANT NOTE ABOUT REFERENCE SECTION: Include only the name, email, and phone number of your Professional References Candidates invited for an on-campus interview may be required to present a teaching lecture and laboratory demonstration of their instructional abilities. Specific questions may be directed to Jason Witherell, Chair of the Department of Engineering, at jwitherell@shawnee.edu or (740)351-3113. The information pertaining to remuneration is found in the Adjunct Faculty Handbook ( Adjunct Handbook (Download PDF reader) ) Adjunct faculty at SSU are also eligible for tuition waivers ( Tuition Waiver for Adjunct Faculty ) and enjoy professional development opportunities, office space, and limited mileage reimbursement. They and their family (children 14 years and up) also have free access to the Rhodes Athletic Facility. Note to Applicants: This is an open posting maintained and updated every semester based upon the enrollment needs of the Department, and as such, is filled on an as-needed/ongoing basis every semester. SSU seeks individuals who share our commitment to students as our first priority. AA/EOE Statement Shawnee State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against any individual because of race, color, genetic information, religion, age, disability, national origin, ancestry, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, veteran status or military status. Minimum Job Knowledge, Skills and Abilities DESIRED BACKGROUND and/or EXPERIENCE Teaching experience in related discipline is preferred. Work experience in related discipline is preferred. Professional certification/licensure/credentials/degree in the respective area when applicable. Minimum Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (EDUCATION, KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES, AND EXPERIENCE) Qualifications can vary depending on experience and courses or programs, but include the following: Bachelor’s, Master’s, Doctorate degree in the respective discipline or related area Ability to use technology in teaching Possess excellent communication skills and ability to communicate effectively with students with a wide range of skills Ability to use collaborative learning techniques and student-centered methods of instruction Ability to work in a multi-ethnic/multicultural environment Ability to work a flexible schedule that includes evening – daytime availability a plus (in some cases may be required) This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
