    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5385764/student-employee-athletics-lifeguard-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Athletics - Lifeguard - 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, Athletics - Lifeguard - 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-686 Division Advancement and Enrollment Management Department AEM-Athletic/Intramurals Opening Date 06/26/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary Athletics department is hiring for the position of Lifeguard - Weight Room Attendant. ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Student Rec Center is multi -purpose hub for physical fitness and social connection for students. The weight room caters to all levels of consumers from casual to elite athletes. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: A lifeguard’s primary duty is to ensure the safety of all swimmers and prevent accidents. They are to maintain continuous surveillance, enforce facility rules, and respond to emergencies. Lifeguard must be currently lifeguard and first aid certified. Hazard Inspections: Check pool equipment and water conditions daily for safety issues. Water Quality: Conduct chemical residual tests (chlorine, pH levels) and log readings as required by local health codes. Facility Maintenance: Keep the pool deck clear of debris, sweep and mop deck, wipe down seating area and help keep clean associated areas like locker rooms. Additional Duties as Front Desk Attendant: Welcome Desk/Access Control: Greeting patrons, verifying student IDs, and managing facility walk-ins. Answering Inquiries: Providing information about fitness classes, intramural sports leagues, building hours, and facility rules Routine Upkeep: Performing frequent walkthroughs to ensure the weight room and cardio areas are free of hazards and stocked with machine cleaning products. Equipment Re-racking: Organizing dumbbells, weight plates, and yoga mats into their proper storage locations. Facility Hygiene: Wiping down exercise machines, cleaning windows or mirrors, and keeping lounge area clean. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5387356/student-employee-math-center-tutor-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Math Center Tutor - 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, Math Center Tutor - 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Regular Job Number POS-647 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-CAS-Mathematics Opening Date 06/26/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Math Center supports SSU students by offering math and statistics tutoring. Additionally, math/stats peer tutors provide support to faculty by helping the students experience success in their math and statistics courses. To support the university community, especially departments with totally online degrees, tutors will provide online tutoring from the Math Center. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: Tutors are responsible for cheerfully greeting and welcoming students as well as assisting them with math and statistics homework. If tutors cannot answer students' questions, then it is the tutor's responsibility to find the course instructor or another faculty member and ask for help. Tutors are not allowed to send students away because they are unfamiliar with the math/stats course concepts. Training will be provided for MicroSoft Office Teams Shifts, the Tutee Survey that students complete at the end of their tutoring session, as well as Bb Ultra Collaborate. • Preferred skills: Math/Stats peer tutors need to have a B or higher in Calculus and/or Stats. • Confidentiality expectations – tutors are not to discuss tutees with other tutors unless it is in real time for helping a student solve problems • Software Knowledge - Familiarity with Blackboard Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5388319/student-employee-athletics-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Athletics 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, Athletics 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-686 Division Advancement and Enrollment Management Department AEM-Athletic/Intramurals Opening Date 06/26/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Athletic Office Worker serves as a support staff member for the Athletics Department by assisting with daily operations, customer service, administrative tasks, and departmental events. This position provides student employees with hands-on experience in collegiate athletics operations, event management, campus engagement, and student support services. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: General Office Support Assist with daily office operations and administrative tasks Answer phones, greet visitors, and provide customer service to guests, students, and staff File documents, organize records, and maintain office materials Assist with data entry, copying, scanning, and other clerical duties Help prepare materials for meetings, recruiting visits, and athletic events Campus Tours and Visitor Engagement Assist with guided campus tours for prospective student-athletes and families Help coordinate recruiting visit schedules and hospitality needs Provide a positive and professional representation of the institution and athletics department Additional Responsibilities Complete other duties as assigned by athletics administration or supervising staff Maintain professionalism and confidentiality within the athletics department Adhere to all institutional, departmental, and NCAA policies and procedures Ability to stand for extended periods during events or tours Ability to lift and move light to moderate equipment and supplies Ability to work in office, athletic facility, and outdoor event environments Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5388462/student-employee-events-setup-crew-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Events Setup Crew 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, Events Setup Crew 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-645 Division Advancement and Enrollment Management Department AEM-Development & Community Engagement Opening Date 06/26/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The University & Community Events Office oversees the Morris University Center and Kricker Innovation Hub Information Desks as well as the scheduling, setting up, tearing down of all internal and external events on Shawnee State University’s campus. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: Assist with daily event management to include unlocking rooms, setting up equipment and furniture for events and maintaining awareness of daily event schedule. Assist with maintaining appearance/cleanliness of spaces across campus. Setup and teardown of tables, chairs, and other equipment for internal and external events on campus for 50+ attendees. Parking attendant. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION: Heavy lifting (up to 50 pounds) May work nights and evenings Must be able to adhere to all safety standards and work practices established by the university. Must be able to stand, walk, lift and move small furniture. Considerable lifting, bending, climbing, and walking are required to successfully do this job. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5415926/student-employee-tutor-student-success-center-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Tutor - Student Success Center 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, Tutor - Student Success Center 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-656 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-Student Success Center Opening Date 07/20/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Student Success Center supports current SSU students by offering free tutoring for the majority of introductory courses. Tutoring can usually be arranged for courses that are not introductory courses provided the Student Success Center can secure a qualified tutor for that subject. Free Supplemental Instruction is also available for currently enrolled SSU students in certain courses. Supplemental Instruction is peer-led study sessions where the SI Leader works closely with the course instructor and may even attend the class being tutored. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: Tutors are responsible for cheerfully greeting and welcoming students as well as assisting them with homework and study skills. If tutors cannot answer students' questions, then it is the tutor's responsibility to find the course instructor or another faculty member and ask for help. Tutors are not allowed to send students away because they are unfamiliar with course concepts. Training will be provided for Microsoft Office Teams Shifts, the student tracker form, as well as Bb Ultra Collaborate. Earned a cumulative GPA of 3.0, and a minimum session GPA of 2.5. Preferred skills: Tutors need to have earned a grade of B or higher in the course being tutored within the last two years Confidentiality expectations – tutors are not to discuss tutees with other tutors unless it is in real time for helping a student solve problems Software Knowledge - Familiarity with Blackboard Ability to keep a brief session log of each tutoring session Minimum Qualifications Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5432301/student-employee-preventative-maintenance-assistant-plastics-engineering-techn": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Preventative Maintenance Assistant - Plastics Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Student Employee, Preventative Maintenance Assistant - Plastics Engineering Technology Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-669 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-Engineering Technologies Opening Date 07/31/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Plastics Engineering Technology Program emphasizes the practical application of engineering principles. The curriculum includes hands-on experience with plastics processing, along with focused study in polymer materials and properties, part and mold design, statistics, and computer-aided design. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: • Acquire, maintain, and operate infrastructures, facilities, and equipment • Provide an environment in which student outcomes can be attained • Maintaining appearance/cleanliness of labs • Maintain technical documentation for ABET Accreditation (both Reading & Writing) • Assist in labs with faculty during scheduled classroom / lab times • Adhere to all safety standards and work practices established by the industry • Assist other students with equipment and student projects • Public speaking giving hands on presentations and demonstrations to industry & group tours • Attend off campus recruiting events • Perform other duties as assigned • Participate in industry-partner laboratory projects, including injection molding trials and material property analysis. • Heavy Lifting (50 pounds) • Attained Sophomore status in the program • Registered full time in the Plastics Engineering Technology and or CAD Program • Technical Documentation (both Reading and Writing technical manuals) • Industrial Lab Equipment (Injection Molding, Extrusion, 3D printing, Materials Testing, Machining, etc.) • Industrial Safety • Demonstrated ability to direction and work with limited supervision Minimum Qualifications Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
