    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5432317/student-employee-cybersecurity-assistant-engineering-technology": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Cybersecurity Assistant - Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Student Employee, Cybersecurity Assistant - Engineering Technology Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-669 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department College of Business & Engineering Technologies Opening Date 07/31/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Engineering Technology Cybersecurity Program focuses on students learning how to detect and defend against network infrastructure attacks by learning how to think like a hacker and how to use the tools hackers use to penetrate network defenses. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: • Maintain and operate equipment in the Cyber classroom, lab, and Noc lab • Assist with faculty in lab during lecture lab scheduled times • Maintain inventory of classroom and lab equipment necessary for student projects • Provide environment in which student success can be attained • Assist other students with equipment and projects during open lab times • Maintain appearance/cleanliness of labs • Attend off campus recruiting events • Comfortable with public speaking and hands on demonstrations to industry and group tours • Perform other duties as assigned • Registered full time in the Information Security (Cybersecurity) Program • Demonstrate ability to follow directions and be a leader • Obtained a minimum of sophomore level Minimum Qualifications Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5435305/student-employee-engineering-technology-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Engineering Technology 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, Engineering Technology 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-669 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department College of Business & Engineering Technologies Opening Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: Engineering Technology focuses on the practical application of engineering technique in the real world. This field leads to exciting and professionally-fulfilling careers that stay on the cutting edge of new advancements. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: • Attend off campus recruiting events • Public speaking giving hands on presentations and demonstrations to industry & group tours • Maintain appearance/cleanliness of classroom and labs • Maintain and organize stock of lab equipment • Create/design projects for demonstrations • Adhere to all safety standards and work practices established in industry and labs • Assist faculty in labs with equipment and classroom projects • Perform other duties as assigned • Currently Enrolled in one of the following programs: Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Game Programming, CAD or Electromechanical Engineering Technology • Public Speaking and hands on demonstrations • Attend Recruiting Events off campus • This position is generally tied to a set of laboratories and classrooms and is often associated with one or more courses or programs in Engineering Technology. Generally, only students with experience in those areas will be considered for the position. Minimum Qualifications Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5449113/student-employee-vrcfa-stage-crew-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, VRCFA Stage Crew 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, VRCFA Stage Crew 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-683 Division Finance and Administration Department AEM-Vern Riffe Center for the Arts Opening Date 08/14/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Vern Riffe Center for the Arts Stage Crew provides technical and backstage support for concerts, theatrical productions, university programs, community events, touring productions, lectures, meetings, and other events presented at or utilizing the VRCFA. This is an as-needed, event-based position with no guaranteed number of hours per week . Work opportunities are determined by the VRCFA event schedule and production requirements. Hours may vary considerably from week to week and throughout the year. Stage Crew members work under the supervision of the VRCFA Production Manager and assist in providing a safe, professional, and efficient environment for visiting artists, university productions, rental clients, and audiences. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: Assist with load-in, setup, operation, changeover, and load-out of performances and events. Load and unload trucks containing scenery, lighting, audio equipment, musical instruments, road cases, and other production equipment. Set up and strike staging, platforms, risers, orchestra equipment, chairs, tables, music stands, curtains, and other event equipment. Assist with the installation, focusing, cabling, operation, and removal of theatrical lighting equipment. Assist with audio equipment, including microphones, speakers, monitors, consoles, cabling, stands, and related equipment. Assist with scenery, props, soft goods, projection/video equipment, and other production elements. Serve as deck crew, running crew, spotlight operator, lighting assistant, audio assistant, stagehand, or other backstage position during performances. Assist VRCFA staff and visiting touring personnel with production requirements. Perform stage changeovers during concerts and other live events. Assist with maintaining clean and organized stages, backstage areas, dressing rooms, control areas, shops, loading areas, and equipment storage spaces. Properly handle, transport, and store VRCFA and Shawnee State University equipment. Minimum Qualifications Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5464625/student-employee-fine-digital-performing-arts-26-27-academic-year": {
      "title": "Student Employee, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts 26-27 Academic Year",
      "description": "Student Employee, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number 202300452 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-CAS-Fine, Digital & Performing Arts Opening Date 08/28/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: The Fine, Digital & Performing Arts (FDPA) Department at Shawnee State University supports academic programs and activities in the visual and performing arts. The department serves students, faculty, staff, and visitors through classes, studios, performances, exhibitions, special events, and day-to-day departmental operations. The student employee will assist the department with routine office, studio, gallery, and event-related needs while gaining practical work experience in a professional university environment. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: The FDPA Student Worker provides flexible support across Fine, Digital & Performing Arts. Student employees may be assigned to one or more areas based on their skills, interests, class schedule, and departmental needs. Assignments may include: OFFICE / DEPARTMENT SUPPORT • Provide coverage of the department office; greet students, faculty, staff, and visitors and provide general information. • Receive and route telephone calls and assist with routine customer service. • Assist with copying, scanning, filing, sorting, data entry, and organizing departmental records and materials. • Assist with Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, and other basic office technology. • Run campus errands; sort, deliver, or distribute departmental materials and mail. • Help maintain bulletin boards, signs, flyers, and other department communications. CERAMICS / ART STUDIO SUPPORT • Assist faculty with setting up, maintaining, organizing, and cleaning ceramics and art studio work areas and equipment as directed. • Organize, label, inventory, and distribute studio supplies, tools, and materials. • Assist with preparing studio spaces for classes and resetting work areas afterward. • Help maintain orderly and safe studio work areas and follow all University and studio safety procedures. GAMING / DIGITAL STUDIO SUPPORT • Assist with the operation, setup, organization, and basic troubleshooting of computers, audiovisual equipment, gaming equipment, and other electronic equipment used by the department. • Assist with maintaining an inventory of technology and studio equipment. • Help prepare gaming and digital studio spaces for classes, demonstrations, projects, or events. • Assist faculty and staff with basic technology-related projects and instructional materials as assigned. THEATRE / PERFORMANCE SUPPORT • Assist with theatre, performance, rehearsal, and event setup and reset. • Help arrange or move approved equipment, tables, chairs, props, signs, and other materials as directed. • Assist with checking, organizing, and maintaining theatre or event equipment and supplies. • Help maintain the appearance and organization of performance, backstage, storage, and public areas. • Some assignments may include evening or weekend performances, rehearsals, or special events. APPLETON GALLERY / EXHIBITION SUPPORT • Assist with preparing the Appleton Gallery and other exhibition spaces for exhibits, receptions, and special events. • Assist with installation and removal of artwork, labels, signage, displays, and exhibition materials under faculty/staff supervision. • Help maintain the organization and appearance of gallery and exhibition spaces. • Assist with receptions, registrations, event setup and cleanup, and greeting visitors. • Assist with promotional materials, including distributing or displaying flyers, posters, and other approved publicity materials. ALL ASSIGNMENTS • Must maintain confidentiality when working with departmental information or records. • Attention to detail and good organizational skills are important. • Depending on assignment, audiovisual, computer troubleshooting, graphic arts, photography, inventory, studio, gallery, theatre, or event experience may be helpful but is not required for every student worker. • Some assignments require standing, walking, bending, reaching, and lifting or moving supplies, artwork, equipment, props, or small furniture. • Students assigned to studios, theatre, gallery installation, or equipment-related work must follow all University and departmental safety practices and faculty/staff instructions. • Work schedules are arranged around the student's classes and departmental needs. • Depending on assignment, work may occur in the department office, ceramics/art studios, gaming/digital studios, Appleton Gallery, theatre/performance spaces, classrooms, storage areas, or other campus locations. • Some gallery, theatre, performance, exhibition, or special-event assignments may require evening or weekend hours. Minimum Qualifications Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/4045435/temporary-position-applicant-pool": {
