    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5338955/workforce-education-navigator-star": {
      "title": "Workforce Education Navigator-STAR",
      "description": "Workforce Education Navigator-STAR Salary $48,512.00 - $54,476.00 Annually Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Full-Time Job Number POS-260 Division Advancement and Enrollment Management Department AEM-Admissions Opening Date 09/16/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Job Description Summary The Adult Workforce Education Navigator plays a vital role in delivering exceptional customer service to learners of all ages applying to credit-bearing and non-credit bearing educational programs at Shawnee State University. This position will be responsible for providing services to residents at the STAR Community Justice Center (CJC) in Franklin Furnace, Ohio. The main goal of the Adult Workforce Education Navigator is to facilitate services related to Admissions, Advising, Financial Aid, the Registrar, and Student Accounts specifically for this underserved population of learners. The Navigator will also provide general information about Shawnee State University. Principal Duties and Responsibilities FUNCTIONS: 1. Enrollment and Student Support 2. Program Evaluation and Reporting 3. Administrative Collaboration DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: 1. Enrollment and Student Support Independent engagement with students and interna/external stakeholders to support enrollment and completion of educational courses and programs offered by Shawnee State at the STAR CJC Handles and processes all in-person meetings, phone calls, and emails to Shawnee State University for the student-residents, triaging questions, processing documents, and resolving concerns Develops and implements application and enrollment processes. Reviews application materials to recommend course or program eligibility to student-residents Provide ongoing career counseling and mentorship to student-residents while at STAR CJC and after re-entry into the community. This includes supporting the student as they navigate any certification and licensure exams and contributing to the educational aspects of their re-entry Evaluate participant needs in order to promote successful outcomes 2. Program Evaluation and Reporting Provides technical expertise with ongoing evaluation of the educational programs and courses offered by SSU at STAR CJC Engages in continuous improvement of processes Makes recommendations for courses and programs based on resident interest and demand Develop and maintain a reporting system to collect, analyze, and regularly report time-and-effort, activities and performance metrics Develop and implement surveys regarding course and career interests, outcomes, and other metrics needed to review, evaluate, and improve student-resident experience Identify opportunities for ITAG, CTAG, or articulation agreements and report to academic areas. 3. Administrative Collaboration Know and adhere to STAR CJC policies and procedures and SSU policies and procedures Communicate with STAR CJC employees to ensure SSU processes align with STAR CJC requirements and policies. Participate in internal committees, working groups, and events to ensure consistency of processes. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Job Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Excellent verbal and written communication skills, Strong interpersonal and customer service skills, Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail, Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in the area of behavioral health, higher education administration, or related field 4-5 years of relevant experience OR Masters degree 2-3 years of relevant experience. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Slate and Jenzabar Shawnee State University offers a competitive starting salary (commensurate with overall qualifications) including an attractive benefits package. See Overview of Employee Benefits for more information. Some of our benefits include: Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break in December Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Tuition Waiver Life Insurance Retirement Plans Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5508819/library-access-specialist-1": {
      "title": "Library Access Specialist 1",
      "description": "Library Access Specialist 1 Salary $14.56 - $20.48 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-1016 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-Clark Memorial Library Opening Date 10/22/2026 Closing Date 11/4/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary JOB PURPOSE STATEMENT Under limited supervision, the Library Specialist I – Access Services staffs the circulation desk, supervises students during evening and weekend hours. This position also manages the 24-hour lab and services independently during evening/early morning; applies library policies, standards, and procedures. Principal Duties and Responsibilities FUNCTIONS: Coordinates activities of the circulation desk, including recording desk statistics. Acts as the evening staff coordinator for the building, as scheduled Performs other duties as assigned DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Coordinates activities of the library service desk Actively assists patrons with check-out and first-line reference questions; assists with patron record issues Communicates knowledge of circulation policies and procedures including OhioLINK and Interlibrary Loan information to diverse patron populations Provides initial troubleshooting and problem-solving to library patrons and transfers unresolved problems to the appropriate staff member or department Has specialized knowledge of automated systems to monitor, maintain, and update patron information Creates new patron records; uses Boolean search techniques for creating lists within the integrated library system; edits patron records as needed Reports critical computer problems to the supervisor for UIS notification Troubleshoots library equipment such as printer/photocopier, scanner, and computers Coordinates and guides student employees in basic circulation duties including opening and closing procedures; checking in/out materials using the system, including OhioLINK and reserve items; proper telephone procedures; finding requested library materials; collecting money and receipt procedures; shelving books and materials Maintains and applies knowledge of Library of Congress Classification System Acts as backup person for OhioLINK/Interlibrary Loan procedures Maintains statistics for Service Desk Acts as the evening and weekend staff coordinator for the building, as scheduled Performs opening and closing routines Responsible for building security and emergency procedures Coordinates creation and delivery of patron notices Performs other duties as assigned Minimum Job Knowledge, Skills and Abilities MINIMUM JOB KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: Knowledge of multiple software products. Ability to assist students, faculty, and staff with computer issues Analytical skills necessary to interpret issues, needs, and library policies Interpersonal skills necessary to provide excellent customer service to students, faculty, and the public Position requires frequent stooping and lifting – able to lift 20-30 pounds to shift resources as necessary Minimum Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE) Associate's degree or equivalent One (1) year related experience Shawnee State University offers a competitive starting salary (commensurate with overall qualifications) including an attractive benefits package. See Overview of Employee Benefits for more information. Some of our benefits include: Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break in December Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Tuition Waiver Life Insurance Retirement Plans Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5525277/head-coach-mens-soccer": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Men's Soccer",
      "description": "Head Coach, Men's Soccer Salary $54,440.80 - $61,245.90 Annually Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Full-Time Job Number POS-350 Division Advancement and Enrollment Management Department AEM-Athletic/Intramurals Opening Date 10/22/2026 Closing Date 11/29/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary This position serves as the Head Coach of SSU’s Men’s Soccer Program. The Head Coach plans and implements training programs to improve players’ skills and performance. Analyze the strengths and weaknesses of opposing teams to develop winning strategies, oversee the physical and mental health of players, ensuring they receive adequate rest, nutrition, and care. Communicate effectively with players, providing feedback and motivation to help them reach their full potential. Coordinate with the team manager and other staff to organize training schedules, travel, and other logistical details. Monitor and maintain discipline, team morale, and cohesion. Help athletes with their personal and athletic development. Recruit, scout, and select talented players for the team. Ensure compliance with league rules and regulations. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Functions: Directs the Men’s Soccer Program Serves as Athletic department liaison for SSU Center for International Programs & Activities Works with the Athletics Game Day & Events Coordinator assisting with summer and off season camps Duties and Responsibilities: Directs Men’s Soccer Program Leads the SSU Soccer Program through planning, direction, and structure to meet the goals of the institution and the team. Ensures the team operates within the guidelines of the University, Mountain East Conference, and the NCAA rules. Provides on-field coaching and game preparation, film evaluation & scouting for both team and individual skill improvement. Develops practice and competition schedules and ensures equipment and facilities are available and maintained. Oversees travel plans, coordinates video, opponent scouting, etc. Responsible for selecting and supervising volunteer and paid assistant coaches, overseeing budgets (operating and scholarship) and execute fundraising plans. Recruits, evaluates, and monitors student athletes who represent Shawnee State well in academics, discipline, and sportsmanship. Motivates athletes to be good examples of the university community. Coordinates, runs, and administers summer camp (individual, team, summer leagues, etc.) programs. Coordinates with regional schools and community groups for scheduling turf usage. Serves as Athletic department liaison for SSU Center for International Programs & Activities Works closely with Center for International Programs & Activities (CIPA) staff in serving international athletes. Maintains compliance and facilitates engagement between international student athletes and other students. Supports activities for international students coming to Shawnee State University and coordinates activities related to employment opportunities for international athletes. Ensures the university establishes goals and objectives for enrollment of international students by working in collaboration with Admissions and CIPA offices. Supports the academic success and personal well-being of international students by assisting them in effectively utilizing the resources of the University and providing leadership. Works with the Athletics Game Day & Events Coordinator and other coaches, assisting with summer and off-season camps Serves as a liaison with the Head Coaches for sports camps, helps manage facility schedules, equipment requests, and camp processes (arrival/dismissal, orientation, etc). Serves as a liaison with camp coordinators regarding schedules, facility coordination, and staff issues. Ensures camp operations run smoothly by remaining in contact with camp staff. Interacts in a positive, professional, and cooperative manner with families and athletic staff; handles appropriate questions or concerns. Minimum Job Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Previous coaching experience at the collegiate level. Knowledge of coaching strategies, recruiting, eligibility rules, River States Conference and NAIA eligibility. Knowledge of the workings of higher education in regard to student retention and progress toward graduation. Good communication skills to speak with recruits, parents, and students. Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor's Degree in Sports Administration/Coaching or related field 2. Two (2) to three (3) years related experience 3. MVR Shawnee State University offers a competitive starting salary (commensurate with overall qualifications) including an attractive benefits package. See Overview of Employee Benefits for more information. Some of our benefits include: Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break in December Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Tuition Waiver Life Insurance Retirement Plans Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5525847/assistant-professor-certificate-and-credential-programs-chhs-rehabilitation-sc": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Certificate and Credential Programs, CHHS- Rehabilitation Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Certificate and Credential Programs, CHHS- Rehabilitation Sciences Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Full-Time Job Number POS-473 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-College of Health & Human Services Opening Date 10/22/2026 Closing Date 1/3/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary The Rehabilitation Sciences Department at Shawnee State University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor, Certificate and Credential Programs, to lead the development, implementation, and evaluation of an innovative Community Health Worker (CHW) education and workforce development program, additional short-term credential programs in behavioral health, and coordination of existing Behavioral Health Paraprofessional Certificate. This position aligns with the institution's commitment to advancing health equity, improving population health outcomes, and addressing workforce shortages across rural and underserved communities. The successful candidate will provide visionary leadership in building a comprehensive CHW training and certification pathway, establishing partnerships with healthcare systems, community-based organizations, public health agencies, and state stakeholders. The faculty member will contribute to teaching, scholarship, community engagement, and workforce development initiatives that strengthen Ohio's behavioral health and healthcare ecosystem and improve access to care. This is a grant-funded position, currently awarded through September 30, 2028. Key Responsibilities: • Design, implement, and continuously improve a Community Health Worker education and training program that aligns with Ohio workforce needs and state requirements. • Develop CHW curriculum, competency frameworks, experiential learning opportunities, and continuing education offerings. • Lead the program approval process, as well as ongoing quality improvement and program evaluation efforts. • Collaborate to ensure recruitment and retention strategies that support student enrollment in certificates and credentials. • Collaborate with academic leadership to expand educational pathways and stackable credentials. • Build and maintain partnerships with healthcare organizations, federally qualified health centers, public health departments, social service agencies, schools, and community-based organizations offering internship/field placement opportunities for certificate and credential programs. • Teach undergraduate and/or professional courses related to the CHW credential and other certificates/credentials as qualified. • Coordinate identification of qualified adjunct faculty for certificate and credential programs. • Advise students involved in certificate and credential programs. • Supervise applied learning experiences/field placements for CHW and BHPP programs • Collaborate with interdisciplinary faculty, the Rural Health Innovation Center, and healthcare partners on research initiatives and potential funding opportunities • Participate in university, college, and departmental service activities. • Represent the institution in statewide and national CHW organizations. • Support workforce development initiatives that expand employment opportunities for CHWs throughout Ohio. The search committee will review applications until the position is filled; however, to ensure best consideration, candidates are encouraged to submit their application by November 15, 2026. Interested candidates must apply online to this Posting by clicking the Apply link above and including: a cover letter addressed to Dr. Tony Ward, Interim Dean, College of Health & Human Services, specifically addressing how your qualifications meet the posted minimum requirements of the position; CV; academic transcripts from all higher education institutions attended (official transcripts will be requested prior to hiring); 1 to 2-page statement of teaching philosophy; in the Professional References section of your application, enter a minimum of three references who can confirm your experience and abilities to perform the responsibilities of this position. Reference letters should be addressed to Dr. Tony Ward, Interim Dean, College of Health & Human Services Candidates invited for an on-campus interview will be required to present a teaching and lab demonstration of their abilities. Specific questions regarding this position may be directed to Dr. Tony Ward, Interim Dean, College of Health & Human Services, at tward@shawnee.edu. Shawnee State University is the regional state university for South-Central Ohio. It is a primarily undergraduate, four-year public university with limited graduate degree programs. Enrollment is approximately 3,500 students. Shawnee State is located on the Ohio River in Portsmouth, Ohio – a small city nestled in a beautiful, rural area of Southern Ohio. Portsmouth is approximately an hour drive from Huntington, WV, and two hours from Columbus or Cincinnati, Ohio. Additional information about SSU is available at www.shawnee.edu . Shawnee State offers a competitive salary (commensurate with experience and qualifications) including an attractive benefits package, Overview of Employee Benefits . Employment with the University is dependent upon BOT budget approval for the fiscal year. Official transcripts and background check are required prior to hire. SSU seeks individuals who share our commitment to students as our first priority. Shawnee State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against any individual because of race, color, genetic information, religion, age, disability, national origin, ancestry, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, veteran status or military status. Minimum Qualifications • Master’s degree or higher in Public Health, Health Education, Community Health, Nursing, Social Work, Health Services Research, Healthcare Administration, or a closely related discipline that meets eligibility to serve as an Ohio CHW training program administrator under Ohio Administrative Code 4723-26-12. • Demonstrated experience working with community health workers, community health programs, population health initiatives, or workforce development efforts. • At least two years’ behavioral health experience • Experience building partnerships with community organizations and healthcare stakeholders. • Strong communication and leadership skills. • Evidence of teaching, training, program development, or community-engaged scholarship. DESIRED BACKGROUND AND EXPERIENCE • Doctoral degree in Public Health, Health Education, Community Health, Nursing, Social Work, Health Services Research, Healthcare Administration, or a closely related discipline that meets Eligibility to serve as an Ohio CHW training program administrator under Ohio Administrative Code 4723-26-12 • Experience developing or directing a Community Health Worker training or certification program • Three or more years’ behavioral health experience • Knowledge of Ohio healthcare systems, public health infrastructure, and workforce development initiatives • Experience securing and managing grant funding • Demonstrated commitment to rural health, health equity, and addressing social determinants of health • Record of peer-reviewed scholarship and interdisciplinary collaboration • Experience evaluating health workforce or community-based interventions Shawnee State University offers a competitive starting salary (commensurate with overall qualifications) including an attractive benefits package. See Overview of Employee Benefits for more information. Some of our benefits include: Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break in December Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Tuition Waiver Life Insurance Retirement Plans Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5443119/operations-manager-adena": {
      "title": "Operations Manager, Adena",
      "description": "Operations Manager, Adena Salary $54,440.00 - $61,245.00 Annually Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Full-Time Job Number POS-966 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-College of Health & Human Services Opening Date 08/10/2026 Description Benefits Job Description Summary The Additional Location Operations Manager serves as the primary institutional representative at Shawnee State’s additional location in Chillicothe, Ohio. They direct and manage the additional location operations at Chillicothe, providing oversight and direction for the operations of all degree and course offerings at this site. The position oversees and directs all processes related to the delivery of SSU programs and courses at the additional location, including: recruitment and enrollment processes for prospective students seeking programs/courses at this location, student and faculty support for enrolled students, and serving as the primary point of contact addressing all operational needs for SSU students, faculty/staff and Adena team members at SSU’s additional location (Chillicothe). Due to the location on the campus of the Adena Regional Medical Center and the primary health care focus of programs, healthcare leadership experience is required. Principal Duties and Responsibilities FUNCTIONS: Strategic Leadership and Operations Management for SSU Additional Location Partnership Development, Student Success. And Community Engagement Assessment, Data Analysis, and Continuous Improvement DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Strategic Leadership and Operations Management for SSU Additional Location Provides strategic leadership, operational oversight, and administrative management for all academic and student support functions at the site. Ensures effective delivery of academic programs, compliance with institutional and accreditation requirements, stakeholder satisfaction, and continuous operational improvement. Directs and manages all operational activities associated with the delivery of academic programs, courses, student services technology resources, facilities coordination, and institutional partnerships at the University’s additional location. Includes being point-of-contact for vendors engaged in service agreements for technology installed at additional location. Exercises independent judgement and decision-making authority regarding day-to-day operations, resource allocation, issue resolution, and stakeholder concerns to ensure uninterrupted delivery of academic programming and student support services. Key internal stakeholders include SSU administrative leadership, faculty, staff and external stakeholders include Adena administration and team members and community partners. Serves as University’s designated on-site administrator and institutional representative, ensuring alignment between University objectives and additional location operations. Coordinates cross-functional operational activities among Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, Informational Technology Services, Facilities, Finance and external partners. Partnership Development, Student Success. And Community Engagement Develops and maintains strategic relationships that support enrollment growth, student success, academic quality, community partnerships, and institutional visibility at the additional location. Serves as primary University representative and relationship manager for all internal and external stakeholders associated with the additional location Develops, coordinates, and implements communication strategies that support enrollment, retention, stakeholder engagement, and effective operations. Implements recruitment and enrollment strategies and processes for SSU programs and courses at additional location in collaboration with CHHS Dean, relevant admissions team members (Director of Admissions, Chief Enrollment Officer, Admissions Associates, Advisors, Financial Aid, Student Accounts, Registrar, key faculty/program directors, etc). Plans, coordinates, and participates in student engagement and recruitment activities at various venues. Cultivates strategic partnerships with healthcare systems, community organizations, workforce partners, educational institutions, and regional employers to enhance program visibility and support enrollment growth. Serves as liaison and resource between all stakeholders, provides support and mentorship for new program/course implementation; ensures student support services are provided and facilitates student engagement at additional location. Other duties as assigned. Identifies barriers affecting student persistence and success and collaborates with university partners to implement solutions and interventions. Assessment, Data Analysis, and Continuous Improvement Uses data-informed decision-making processes to evaluate operational effectiveness, student outcomes, stakeholder satisfaction, enrollment trends and program success at the additional location. Develops, implements, and monitors performance metrics and assessment processes to evaluate operational effectiveness and support institution/program reporting requirements. Ensures alignment with university policies and procedures, and supports compliance with HLC requirements for additional location. Analyzes operational, enrollment, retention, and student success data; recommends and implements improvements that enhance service quality, efficiency, and student outcomes Prepares reports, recommendations, and strategic planning information for University leadership regarding additional location performance and future growth opportunities Minimum Job Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to work collaboratively within SSU systems and with external stakeholders to provide leadership for the implementation of additional location program/course offerings. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills Ability to independently manage multiple tasks, prioritize effectively, and work in a fast-paced environment Excellent organizational and problem-solving skills, as well as attention to detail Minimum Qualifications Minimum required: Bachelors in Health Care Administration, Business Administration, Higher Ed Administration, Organizational Leadership or related field. Degrees in health discipline also acceptable. Must have 5 years of progressively responsible professional experience and 3 years of leadership, supervisory, project management, or operational management experience. Healthcare leadership experience is required. University driving approval Preferred: Masters degree in Healthcare Administration, Business Administration, Public Administration, Higher Education Administration, or Organizational Leadership. Experience in higher education. Experience in healthcare administration, Experience managing external and multiple stakeholder partnerships. Experience supporting academic program implementation. Directly relevant clinical and/or leadership experience in health field, preferably 5+ years in leadership role Strong understanding of and demonstrated ability to lead implementation of new initiatives Higher education work experience If health care provider, current licensure/credential preferred but not required. Working Conditions: This position is based in Chillicothe, with travel as needed to Portsmouth and outreach locations, occasional evening/weekend work for outreach. Normal office environment with little exposure to excessive dust, noise, heat and the like. Some lifting (up to 30 lbs.), walking, and driving required. Valid driver’s license with less than 3 moving violations. Travel and work evenings and/or weekends as needed for recruitment and outreach events. Work schedule adjusted accordingly. Shawnee State University offers a competitive starting salary (commensurate with overall qualifications) including an attractive benefits package. See Overview of Employee Benefits for more information. Some of our benefits include: Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break in December Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Tuition Waiver Life Insurance Retirement Plans Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply"
    }
  },
